  "article": {
    "headline": "Why window light feels soft",
    "answer": "A large window spreads light over a wider area than a small lamp. Shadows soften because light can reach the subject from many directions.\n\nCloud cover makes the effect stronger. The sky becomes an even source of light, so the difference between highlights and shadows is smaller.\n\nTry moving a cup toward the window and then away from it. Watch the edge of its shadow. That edge tells you more about the light than the brightness of the room."
  },
